{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1494534-scion-origin-power-level","id":1494534,"title":"Scion Origin power level","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-07T10:48:02-07:00","id":1494534,"title":"Scion Origin power level","content":"Hello. Could someone comment on the general power level of characters in Scion Origin? Also, I am a little confused on how Origin and Hero fit with each other. Is it often the case where a play group starts a Origin level story and then the characters through experience points advance to Hero level story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27612-awesomeotter","name":"Awesomeotter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T12:49:09-07:00","id":1494545,"title":"","content":"Scion Origin is like... Did you run Chronicles of Darkness ( 1st or 2nd Edition), particularly? It's like Mortal games, but with competent ( 4 dots) mortal characters. Scion Hero is like at least like supernatural monsters game - maybe even more with divine interventions from time to time. Or 'Percy Jackson for adults'. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T14:02:36-07:00","id":1494555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1494534-scion-origin-power-level?p=1494545#post1494545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion Origin is like... Did you run Chronicles of Darkness ( 1st or 2nd Edition), particularly? It's like Mortal games, but with competent ( 4 dots) mortal characters. Scion Hero is like at least like supernatural monsters game - maybe even more with divine interventions from time to time. Or 'Percy Jackson for adults'. \ud83d\ude0e</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Origin characters are basically to help you get a feel for your character by playing around with them pre-visitation doing stuff that is in the bounds of mortal power (with the occasional act of divine intervention hinting at your parent watching out for you and guiding you to become ready to become a hero via omens). I'd wager a lot of people skip this step entirely and just start out as already having been visited by their divine parent and being a hero with cool magic powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T11:25:34-07:00","id":1494617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Awesomeotter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1494534-scion-origin-power-level#post1494534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello. Could someone comment on the general power level of characters in Scion Origin? Also, I am a little confused on how Origin and Hero fit with each other. Is it often the case where a play group starts a Origin level story and then the characters through experience points advance to Hero level story?</div> </div> </div> </div>Origin characters are humans with &quot;something&quot; extra that makes them very competent in several areas, and also gives them a bit of supernatural luck. Usually they're more powerful than other humans, but against supernatural denizens they tend to be on the disadvantage. Hero is when you start to kick ass, most encounters with regular humans exist to show just how cool you are, and you can defeat some supernatural creatures all on your own. <br /> Another way of seeing it is that origin characters can reach the peak of human potential, while a hero character can surpass it. It's the difference between a human being doing something amazing but (allegedly) possible and doing something that no regular human could pull off, no matter how much skill and luck it has.<br /> You don't need to start in Origin and then jump to hero, each tier (Origin, Hero, Demigod, God) is designed to play independently if that's what you want. It all boils down to what kind of stories do you want to tell; Origin stories are usually about mystery and self-discovery, while Hero are usually about creating your legend with epic deeds. If you're new, I would recommend starting on Origin, so you can get used to the world and the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 10-08-2022, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T01:32:38-07:00","id":1494779,"title":"","content":"So having just picked up Origin my expectation is that starting PCs are roughly at the level of Hunter: the Reckoning (pre-reboot). That is that you have a neat trick or two, and maybe a slightly magical walking stick, but any actual serious threats will crush you into a pancake in a straight up fight. On the other hand your stuff can also be a little bit more weird or explicitly magical, because starting with Birthrights are an option I've had the idea of a chosen Scion of Nauda with an enchanted prosthetic hand (provided by a cult instead of directly, we are talking pre-vusitation after all).<br /> <br /> You could run an entire game at Origin level, it's versatile enough. But it's not really why you bought the game is it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 10-11-2022, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}